      }
    },
    "A look back on the day, ending with a song to Mary." : {
      "comment" : "Prayers tab, home's hour row: one short line saying what an order of prayer of the day is, under its name",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un repaso del día, que termina con un canto a María."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A meditation on each mystery, to read or to hear" : {
      "comment" : "Onboarding, What the app holds slide: one line naming something the app offers",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una meditación sobre cada misterio, para leer o escuchar"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mystery is a moment in the life of Jesus and Mary — His birth, His agony in the garden, His rising. There are twenty, in four sets of five. Each day has its own set, and the Luminous can be prayed any day you choose. While your lips say the Hail Marys of a decade, your mind stays with its mystery." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, lesson 3, The Mysteries: the lesson's opening paragraphs; a blank line divides them",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un misterio es un momento de la vida de Jesús y de María: su nacimiento, su agonía en el huerto, su resurrección. Son veinte, en cuatro series de cinco. Cada día tiene su serie, y los Luminosos pueden rezarse el día que elijas. Mientras tus labios dicen las avemarías de una decena, tu mente permanece en su misterio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new set" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una serie nueva"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new set, begun with %@" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
