    },
    "Each Hail Mary is a rose. Fifty make a crown." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification in May, the month of Mary: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada avemaría es una rosa. Cincuenta forman una corona."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each Rosary you pray is counted here, by its mysteries." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Aquí se cuenta cada Rosario que reces, por sus misterios."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each day" : {
      "comment" : "Consecration introduction, page 3: kicker over the title, shown in capitals",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada día"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each day has its own mysteries: scenes from the lives of Jesus and Mary to reflect on as you pray. Start today's Rosary here." : {
      "comment" : "First-use tour: a coach mark's words beside the featured card of today's mysteries on home, saying what it is and what it does",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada día tiene sus propios misterios: escenas de la vida de Jesús y de María para meditar mientras rezas. Comienza aquí el Rosario de hoy."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each day you pray adds one" : {
      "comment" : "Chapel, Prayer Streak tile: italic line under the figure when there is no next milestone",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada día que rezas suma uno"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each day you pray adds one to your streak." : {
      "comment" : "Streak card: the line before any streak has begun",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada día que rezas suma uno a tu racha."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each hidden word keeps its first letter" : {
      "comment" : "Chant practice settings, under Hide words",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada palabra oculta conserva su primera letra"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each mystery has its fruit — the grace, by long tradition, to ask for while its decade is prayed. The cards name it under Ask for." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada misterio tiene su fruto: la gracia que, por larga tradición, se pide mientras se reza su decena. Las tarjetas la nombran bajo Pide."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each mystery in the Gospel" : {
      "comment" : "Chapel, Library tile: line under the In Scripture door",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada misterio en el Evangelio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each mystery teaches a virtue — humility, patience, faith. Ask for it as you begin the ten Hail Marys." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, lesson 3, How to dwell on a mystery: what way III means",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada misterio enseña una virtud: humildad, paciencia, fe. Pídela al comenzar las diez avemarías."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each mystery's passage" : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, Going Deeper: line under In Scripture",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El pasaje de cada misterio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Each mystery, a scene from the lives of Jesus and Mary, is told verse by verse. The Our Father bead names the mystery and a grace to ask for, each of the Hail Marys has its own verse, and the Glory Be closes it." : {
      "comment" : "The Scriptural Rosary's own page, ledger: what the form is",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cada misterio, una escena de la vida de Jesús y de María, se narra versículo a versículo. La cuenta del Padrenuestro nombra el misterio y una gracia que pedir, cada avemaría tiene su propio versículo, y el Gloria lo cierra."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Early Morning Prayer" : {
      "comment" : "Hours of Prayer (the Divine Office): an hour of prayer's plain name, the app's title for it; never 'Morning Prayer' or 'Night Prayer', which are other prayers in the app",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Oración de primera hora"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Easter is not one day. Keep it with a decade." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification in the Easter season: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "La Pascua no es un solo día. Vívela con una decena."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Easter to Pentecost" : {
      "comment" : "Prayers tab: the part of the year a seasonal song to Mary is sung, in plain dates (February 2 is Candlemas)\nStreak milestone: what the Church calls a run of this many days of prayer, lower case, shown after the count, like 9 days · a novena",
      "localizations" : {
