    },
    "Eight centuries of saints have not exhausted the mysteries." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers learning the Rosary: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ocho siglos de santos no han agotado los misterios."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Eight prayers make the whole Rosary, and most of them you may already half know. Read each one through. Then try “Say it with me”: the prayer comes a line at a time, so you can say each line before you see it.\n\nStart with the Hail Mary. It is said fifty-three times in one Rosary, and after a week it will be yours." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, lesson 2, The Prayers: the lesson's opening paragraphs; a blank line divides them",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ocho oraciones forman todo el Rosario, y quizá ya conozcas a medias la mayoría. Lee cada una completa. Luego prueba “Dila conmigo”: la oración aparece línea por línea, para que digas cada línea antes de verla.\n\nComienza con el Ave María. Se reza cincuenta y tres veces en un Rosario, y en una semana será tuya."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Eight prayers make the whole Rosary. Read them, then say them with the page until they are yours." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray: one line under the title of lesson 2, The Prayers",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ocho oraciones forman todo el Rosario. Léelas y luego dilas con la página hasta que sean tuyas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
