          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One bead at a time" : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers drawn by peace and stillness: its title, shown in bold. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 35 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una cuenta a la vez"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One gentle reminder a day, at the hour you choose" : {
      "comment" : "Onboarding, What the app holds slide: one line naming something the app offers",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un recordatorio sencillo al día, a la hora que elijas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One question to sit with, and a journal to answer it in." : {
      "comment" : "Consecration introduction, page 3: what the day's third step, Reflect, holds",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una pregunta para meditar, y un diario para responderla."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One short note, when you finish a Rosary prayed with meditations: which meditations they were, and whether you listened to the Whole Rosary. Our server keeps it with the time and an approximate city, region and country, looked up through ipapi.co from the address your phone connects from, and keeps that address only in a shortened form. No name, account or device identifier goes with it, so two Rosaries prayed on one phone look like two prayed by strangers. We use these notes only to learn which meditations are prayed, and roughly where. The Scriptural Rosary, the Audio Rosary and the guided Rosary send nothing, and nothing else reaches us unless you write to us." : {
      "comment" : "Privacy Policy: a section's text; keep it as plain and exact as the English",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Una breve nota, cuando terminas un Rosario rezado con meditaciones: cuáles meditaciones fueron, y si escuchaste el Rosario completo. Nuestro servidor la guarda con la hora y una ciudad, región y país aproximados, obtenidos mediante ipapi.co a partir de la dirección desde la que se conecta tu teléfono, y guarda esa dirección solo en forma abreviada. No va con ella ningún nombre, cuenta ni identificador del dispositivo, así que dos Rosarios rezados en un mismo teléfono parecen rezados por dos desconocidos. Usamos estas notas solo para saber qué meditaciones se rezan, y más o menos dónde. El Rosario bíblico, el Rosario en audio y el Rosario guiado no envían nada, y nada más nos llega a menos que nos escribas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One verse of Scripture for every Hail Mary." : {
      "comment" : "The Scriptural Rosary's own page: the italic line under its name",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un versículo de la Escritura para cada avemaría."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One warm tone with a soft shimmer" : {
      "comment" : "Settings, Reminder Sound: what the sound is like",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Un tono cálido con un suave destello"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Open" : {
      "comment" : "Chapel, Consecration tile: the act at the foot for a preparation chosen ahead (shown in capitals)\nChapel, Journal tile at half width: the act at the foot, opening the journal (shown in capitals)",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
