    "The Rosary" : {
      "comment" : "A meditation set's page: small capitals over the set's name when its mysteries are not known\nDaily prayers list (the rule of prayer): the short name of a devotional act, as a ledger row sets it\nSettings: a section heading",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary asks for no fasting, only a little time." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification in Lent: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario no pide ayuno, solo un poco de tiempo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary asks little and gives much." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers building a daily habit: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario pide poco y da mucho."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary begins at the first mystery and ends at the last Glory Be." : {
      "comment" : "Settings, Opening and Closing Prayers: the line under the chosen option",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario comienza en el primer misterio y termina en el último Gloria."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary begins with the Sign of the Cross and the Creed and ends with the Hail, Holy Queen, each with its words." : {
      "comment" : "Settings, Opening and Closing Prayers: the line under the chosen option",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario comienza con la Señal de la Cruz y el Credo y termina con la Salve, cada una con sus palabras."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is a prayer drawn from the Gospels. It is prayed in five decades — sets of ten Hail Marys. For each decade we call to mind one scene from the life of Jesus and His Mother — a mystery — and while we think about it, we pray: an Our Father, ten Hail Marys, a Glory Be, and the Fatima Prayer.\n\nThe words are simple and the same each time, and that is the point. They become a quiet rhythm under the heart, leaving the mind free to look at Christ. The beads keep the count, so you do not have to." : {
      "comment" : "How to Pray, lesson 1, The Beads and the Order: the lesson's opening paragraphs; a blank line divides them",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario es una oración tomada de los Evangelios. Se reza en cinco decenas, grupos de diez avemarías. En cada decena recordamos una escena de la vida de Jesús y de su Madre —un misterio— y, mientras pensamos en ella, rezamos un Padrenuestro, diez avemarías, un Gloria y la Oración de Fátima.\n\nLas palabras son sencillas y siempre las mismas, y de eso se trata. Se vuelven un ritmo sereno bajo el corazón y dejan la mente libre para mirar a Cristo. Las cuentas llevan el conteo, para que tú no tengas que hacerlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is always the same prayer: the same mysteries in the same order, with ten Hail Marys for each. A meditation set gives you words to think about while you pray.\n\nEach set has one meditation for each mystery: five for the Rosary, or seven for the Seven Sorrows." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario es siempre la misma oración: los mismos misterios en el mismo orden, con diez avemarías en cada uno. Una serie de meditaciones te da palabras en las que pensar mientras rezas.\n\nCada serie tiene una meditación para cada misterio: cinco para el Rosario, o siete para los Siete Dolores."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is at the heart of the app. Around it are other prayers of the Church." : {
      "comment" : "Onboarding, What You Will Find slide: the line under its title when no reason was chosen",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario está en el corazón de la app. A su alrededor hay otras oraciones de la Iglesia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is close by" : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers who gave no reason: its title, shown in bold. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 35 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario está cerca"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is five decades — sets of ten Hail Marys — each spent with one scene from the life of Jesus and Mary. Today's are chosen for you; you may pick others." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario tiene cinco decenas —grupos de diez avemarías—, y cada una se dedica a una escena de la vida de Jesús y de María. Los de hoy ya están elegidos para ti; puedes elegir otros."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is here whenever you are ready." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers who gave no reason: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario está aquí cuando quieras."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary is simply time spent with her." : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayer reminder notification for readers wanting to grow closer to Mary: its text under the title. Warm and inviting, never scolding; under about 75 characters",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario es simplemente tiempo con ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Rosary's own month" : {
