      }
    },
    "The Scriptural Rosary" : {
      "comment" : "Explore page and search: the name of a door to a page of the app\nHow to Pray, Going Deeper: tile opening the Scriptural Rosary's page\nName of the form of the Rosary with a Bible verse for every Hail Mary, as headers and the Lock Screen show it\nPray button tray and its editor: the name of a devotional act the Pray button can open",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario bíblico"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Scriptural Rosary, with a verse for every bead" : {
      "comment" : "Onboarding, What the app holds slide: one line naming something the app offers",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El Rosario bíblico, con un versículo para cada cuenta"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Scripture passage for the mystery, then a few lines of meditation on it.\n\nThe Seven Sorrows are set this way, because the Gospel tells the whole scene. For a verse on every bead, open any of the mysteries and choose The Scriptural Rosary, above the meditations." : {
      "comment" : "Kinds of Meditation sheet, the Gospel card: what this kind of meditation is, then after a blank line some authors who wrote it (keep the names; the blank line stays)",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El pasaje de la Escritura del misterio y luego unas líneas de meditación sobre él.\n\nLos Siete Dolores se presentan así, porque el Evangelio cuenta toda la escena. Para un versículo en cada cuenta, abre cualquiera de los misterios y elige El Rosario bíblico, arriba de las meditaciones."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Seven Sorrows of Mary" : {
      "comment" : "Daily prayers list (the rule of prayer): the short name of a devotional act, as a ledger row sets it\nHome, the featured card under TODAY'S MYSTERIES: the day's devotion with its article\nPray button tray and its editor: the name of a devotional act the Pray button can open",
      "localizations" : {
